# R — analysis project and renv

## renv

This repository **does** use `renv`. The lockfile is the source of truth
for CRAN and Bioconductor versions.

```r
# once, from the project root
renv::init()                 # or renv::restore() on a fresh clone
renv::snapshot()             # after adding packages
```

- Commit `renv.lock` and `renv/activate.R`. Do not commit `renv/library/`.
- Record Bioconductor with `renv::install("bioc::DESeq2")` (and peers).
- Install local/GitHub DeCovarT explicitly, then snapshot.
- Do **not** set `RENV_CONFIG_AUTOLOADER_ENABLED=FALSE` here (that flag
  belongs to the **package** repo, which does not use renv).
- Never call `install.packages()` from analysis scripts or book chunks
  that run on CI; declare packages via `renv::install()` + snapshot.

## Pre-commit

Before every commit or `pre-commit run`:

```bash
pre-commit clean
git add -u   # stage everything you mean to commit
pre-commit run
git add -u   # re-stage if autofix hooks rewrote files
git commit
```

Autofix hooks fail once while rewriting; re-stage. Do not use
`--no-verify` unless the user asks. Prefer `pre-commit clean` over
skipping hooks.

## Project roles

- **`scripts/`:** one-off pipelines (download, GRN, DE, GA, sensitivity).
  Run with vanilla `Rscript --no-save --no-restore` from the **repository
  root**. Use `file.path(...)` from that root (`data/raw/`, `output/`,
  …). Do not `setwd()`. Optional CLI flags are `key=value` on
  `commandArgs(trailingOnly = TRUE)` inside the script that needs them.
- **`docs/`:** Quarto **book** (narrative + figures). Heavy computation
  lives in `scripts/`; the book reads saved artefacts.

### Simulation / pipeline script header

At the top of each long `scripts/*.R` file, document a background `nohup`
invocation (from
[GastroDeconv2FateMap](https://github.com/bastienchassagnol/GastroDeconv2FateMap)):

```r
# mkdir -p logs
# nohup Rscript --no-save --no-restore scripts/<name>.R \
#   > "logs/<stem>_$(date +%F)_<slug>.log" 2>&1 &
```

Bannered sections for Outline (title line ending in ` ----`):

```r
# ==========================================================================
# SECTION 0 · Dependencies and paths ----
# ==========================================================================
```

Number sections 0 (dependencies), 1 (inputs), 2 (method), 3 (outputs)
unless a script needs extra subsections.

## Air, lintr, and style

- Format R with **[Air](https://posit-dev.github.io/air/)** (line width
  **80**, indent **2 spaces**) when `air.toml` is present.
- Follow the [tidyverse style guide](https://style.tidyverse.org/).
- Native pipe `|>`; `package::function()` for non-base functions.
- Assign with `<-`. **Never `<<-`**.
- `glue::glue()` for assigned strings; for `stop()` / `warning()` /
  `message()`, pass parts as separate arguments (never `stop(paste(…))`).
- `TRUE` / `FALSE` only (never `T` / `F`).
- Seeds: scripts and book chunks **should** set a seed
  (`withr::with_seed()`). Do not hide a global `set.seed()` inside a
  helper unless the caller passes `seed`.
- Console: `message()` / `warning()` / `stop()` in helpers; scripts may
  print progress if gated by `verbose`.
- Do not leave `options()`, `par()`, or `setwd()` changed; restore with
  `on.exit()` or **`withr`**.
- Write outputs under `output/` or `data/intermediate/` with explicit
  paths; never to the home filespace by default.
- Cores on CI / book render: at most **2**.
- `requireNamespace("pkg")` to test optional packages; never
  `installed.packages()`.

### dplyr (inside helpers)

- Embrace data-masking args with `{{ var }}`.
- Character names: `.data[[var]]`, `dplyr::all_of()`.

### Plotting (when used)

- Faceted ggplot2: `theme_minimal()` family; horizontal numeric axes.
- Save with `ggplot2::ggsave()` (`limitsize = FALSE`, typically 320 dpi).
- ADEMP-style summaries and rainclouds: reuse DeCovarT helpers when they
  already exist (`DeCovarT::plot_mc_forest()`, `plot_mc_raincloud()`).
- Static tables in the book: `tinytable::tt()`.
- Heatmaps: `ggplot2::geom_tile()` first; `ComplexHeatmap` only for
  genuinely multi-modal displays.

### Parallelism

Prefer **`furrr`** with `furrr::furrr_options(seed = TRUE)` for Monte
Carlo. Never nest parallelism (scenario loop sequential; inner sample
loop may use workers).

