# Bibliography

Keep **two citation streams**. Do not mix them. Do **not** invent BibTeX
entries, citekeys, or DOIs.

## A. Literature (Zotero → Git)

Source of truth: the author's
[Zotero library](https://www.zotero.org/bastienchassagnol/library).
Add items in Zotero first, then export.

From **Zotero 8 onward**, citation keys live in `zotero.sqlite`. Export
into `bibliography/REFERENCES.bib`, then run the DeCovarT hygiene CLI
(or a copy under `scripts/curate_bibliography/` if vendored here):

```bash
python3 ../DeCovarT/scripts/curate_bibliography/check_bibliography.py --clean
```

Library ID: `7172053`. Assign **exactly one** Zotero collection — the
most specific leaf. Do not also attach ancestors.

**Zotero → Git:** export → `--clean` (allowed fields only; DOI-dedupe).

**Git/docs → Zotero:** `zotc keys extract` then `collection add` (dry-run
first).

| Path | Consumer |
|------|----------|
| `bibliography/REFERENCES.bib` | Quarto book (literature) |

Allowed fields: `title`, `author`, `editor`, `year`, `journal`,
`booktitle`, `publisher`, `howpublished`, `doi`, `volume`, `number`,
`pages`, `isbn`, `issn`, `edition`, `school`, `institution`, `url`.

Required fields by type (`utils::bibentry`):

- `@article` — `title`, `author`, `year`, `journal`
- `@book` — `title`, `year`, `publisher`, plus `author` **or** `editor`
- `@incollection` — `title`, `author`, `year`, `booktitle`, `publisher`
- `@phdthesis` / `@mastersthesis` — `title`, `author`, `year`, `school`
- `@techreport` — `title`, `author`, `year`, `institution`

Enrich missing fields with Crossref (`bib_enrich.py`) **without
overwriting** existing values and **without inventing DOIs**. Then
`bibtex-tidy`. Review ambiguous matches by hand.

## B. Software (`packages.bib` — not Zotero)

Regenerate from packages actually used in `docs/` and `scripts/`:

```bash
Rscript scripts/curate_bibliography/generate_packages_bib.R
```

| Path | Consumer |
|------|----------|
| `bibliography/packages.bib` | Quarto book (software) |

## C. Quarto YAML (always two bibliographies)

Every `docs/*.qmd` (or the book-level `_quarto.yml`) must declare:

```yaml
bibliography:
  - ../bibliography/packages.bib
  - ../bibliography/REFERENCES.bib
link-citations: true
```

Example: literature `@suppingerMultimodalCharacterizationMurine2023`;
software `@R-DESeq2`, `@R-huge`, `@R-DeCovarT`.

